s located at $(6,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/state.json" "file_sha256" "7fa7bb211817ee62f856a7dab7c884db5d65bb38d660a4e8119b8e896b812d87" "basis" 892 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "62dce0bec929801edebfbbf1fe08dc7eb7131a05544044744aa1ad1420d64268" "basis" 892 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/state.json" "file_sha256" "7fa7bb211817ee62f856a7dab7c884db5d65bb38d660a4e8119b8e896b812d87" "basis" 892 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981529/state.j