rse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-16461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "978ad4aecbb5087179a1a9a0986edf59e95f7dc95ee797b6f0b5822accb9c3f1"} {"question" "q-16461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-16461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,-2)"] ["math" "(-1,2)"] ["math" "(-2,1)"] ["math" "(1,-2)"] ["math" "(2,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-16461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{49}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{7}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=6$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(6,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "978ad4aecbb5087179a1a9a0986edf59e95f7dc95ee797b6f0b5822accb9c3f1"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278401" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{11}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-7$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(-7,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=11.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=11,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{11}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{11},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{11}=2\\sqrt{11},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "978ad4aecbb5087179a1a9a0986edf59e95f7dc95ee797b6f0b5822accb9c3f1"} {"question" "q-278402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c4141991ce4beb062"} {"question" "q-278402" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/state.json" "file_sha256" "583d196f49dcc52efd388e346e3d5f96473286b07fef0c6c